These documents are SYNTHETIC. They were generated for this assignment and
describe a fictional company. Northwind Traders is Microsoft's long-standing
sample company name, but Microsoft's public Northwind dataset is a relational
database of orders and products -- not prose documents -- so it cannot be used
with a text-chunking RAG pipeline. No real Northwind document corpus was found.

Nothing here is real business information. Do not cite it as such.

Written to be a useful RAG test corpus specifically:

- Six documents on distinct topics, so retrieval has to discriminate between
  them rather than always returning the only thing present.
- Deliberate overlaps -- shipping rules appear in both the shipping terms and
  the support handbook -- so multi-document retrieval can be observed.
- Specific, checkable facts (30-day returns, 15% restocking fee, net 45 terms)
  so an answer can be graded right or wrong rather than judged on tone.
- Facts no language model can know, since the company does not exist. An answer
  that gets them right can only have come from retrieval.

This NOTICE has no file extension so that ingest_corpus.py does not index it.
